# No duplicate template prompts

Before creating **any** new gallery template / live page under `src/templates/`:

1. Read every existing `**/prompt.js` (and `meta.fullPrompt` in the registry).
2. Compare the **new prompt text** to existing ones (trim only; do **not** “normalize” meaning — if the body is the same design prompt, it counts as a duplicate).
3. If a match (or near-identical copy with only title/version wording changed, e.g. “3D Portfolio” vs “3D Portfolio 2.0” with the **same** Build/GLOBAL STYLES body) already exists:

**STOP. Do not implement.**

Reply with a short block message, for example:

> **Blocked — duplicate prompt.**  
> This prompt already ships as **`<existing title>`** (`id: <id>`, path: `src/templates/<category>/<id>/`).  
> Same design prompt must not be built twice. Reuse that template, or change the prompt/content first.

## Allowed

- New tab/category with a **different** prompt
- Fixes/refactors of the **existing** template that owns that prompt
- Explicit user override: only if they say they want a deliberate fork **and** acknowledge the duplicate

## Not allowed

- Creating `3D Portfolio 2.0` (or any rename) that copies an existing `prompt.js` body
- “Slightly different folder name” with the same prompt string
